  "Question": "Calculate: \\(15 \\div 50 \\times 100 = ?\\)",
  "Choices": {},
  "Correct Answer": "30",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "Method 1: Use the percentage relationship\n\n15 is \\(30\\%\\) of 50. Since \\(30\\%=\\frac{30}{100}\\), this means \\(15\\div50=\\frac{30}{100}\\). Multiplying the quotient by \\(100\\) gives\n\\[\n15\\div50\\times100=\\frac{30}{100}\\times100=30.\n\\]\n\nMethod 2: Compute the decimal quotient, then multiply by 100\n\nMultiplication and division have equal priority, so evaluate from left to right. First \\(15\\div50=0.3\\). Multiplying by \\(100\\) moves the decimal point two places to the right, so\n\\[\n15\\div50\\times100=0.3\\times100=30.\n\\]",
